    "note": "candidate-001 feedback fixed. (1) QUANTIZATION (desktop rows + stretched icon box): switched the WHOLE chrome to placeRects (exact-pixel rects packed onto few layers with importance z-order) — icons are exact squares, reviewer discs are true circles, no row drift. m0 208K -> 114K, fewer layers (the perf win). (2) PORTRAIT cramping: text is now width-capped fixed fonts (was fit:contain, which scales to height then CLIPS width on long strings), and narrow/portrait drops the reviewer discs + PR and gives the title its own full-width line. Header title + subtitle + author all width-capped now. (3) ALSO converted the stat-card (it was using placeRect-alone, same bloat) to placeRects — m0 ~16K -> 4K, 25 tests green, geometry identical (glyph still exact-square-centered). Render one-liners in .scratch/share.md.",
